                <pb facs="1110" n="1085" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v08/pg1085"/>

                <head>490. Telegram From the Delegation to the Foreign Ministers Meeting to the
                    Department of State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d490-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-07-29T10:00:00+01:00">July 29, 1959, 10
                            a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Secto 414. In discussion yesterday by Western Foreign Ministers of text contained
                    in Secto 410,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d490-f2"/> following qualifications made: <list>
                        <label>1)</label>
                        <item>Lloyd reserved right to reopen for possible later deletion “and the
                            agreements at present in force” in final sentence introductory
                            paragraph. Other three Ministers all opposed deletion.</item>
                        <label>2)</label>
                        <item>Foreign Ministers agreed declaration of intention in second part
                            sub-paragraph (A) might, if necessary, be changed to direct declaration
                            that governments would limit combined total of their forces, etc.</item>
                        <label>3)</label>
                        <item>Foreign Ministers agreed that final two sentences of sub-paragraph (C)
                            might be eliminated, if in course of discussion with Gromyko removal of
                            quadripartite commission with respect access necessary to combat
                            insistence by Gromyko on commission for other aspects of
                            agreement.</item>
                        <pb facs="1111" n="1086" xml:id="pg1086"/>
                        <label>4)</label>
                        <item>Germans reserved right to press later for elimination of language “or
                            amount to interference in the internal affairs of others” in
                            subparagraph (D).</item>
                        <label>5)</label>
                        <item>Foreign Ministers agreed they would be prepared to drop “in the
                            absence of reunification” in sub-paragraph (E) if necessary in course of
                            negotiations.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
